<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Behavioral Capture and Entropic Authoritarianism: An RSVP Interpretation of Jacob Ward</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Jacob Ward‚Äôs critique of artificial intelligence is not merely sociological‚Äîit is thermodynamic. His central warning, that predictive AI coupled with behavioral science collapses human autonomy into ‚Äúa world without choices,‚Äù describes a deeper distortion of the informational and energetic fields that make cognition, agency, and collective sense-making possible. The Relativistic Scalar‚ÄìVector Plenum (RSVP) formalism makes this pathology explicit: authoritarianism is not only political‚Äîit is a phase transition in the geometry of shared meaning.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">In RSVP, cognition and society arise from the interaction of a scalar entropy field Œ¶ (informational openness, adaptive potential, semantic diversity) and a vector agency field ùíó (directed intent, communicative flow, coordinated action). Freedom is neither metaphysical nor psychological: it is the capacity of a system to sustain non-degenerate entropy gradients while preserving bidirectional vector flow. Ward‚Äôs ‚Äúworld without choices‚Äù is the collapse of this balance into a fixed point‚Äîa state of scalar flattening and vector monodirectionality, where the manifold of possible futures is compressed at the source, rather than explored by agents.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Behavioral science, once a tool for self-understanding, becomes in Ward‚Äôs account an instrument for entropy inversion. By modeling cognition as stimulus‚Äìresponse, it treats choice as a function to be optimized against. Commercial AI operationalizes this assumption, replacing deliberation with prediction and semantic exploration with segmentation. In RSVP terms, this is the deliberate creation of negative scalar curvature wells‚Äîattractors that trap vector flow into repetitive affective vortices such as outrage, identity threat, and tribal self-reinforcement. These are not narratives; they are topological pathologies‚Äîcirculation without escape, motion without evolution, coherence without truth.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The corporate consolidation of AI power that Ward emphasizes corresponds to the emergence of vector field monopoles. A healthy plenum maintains agency through reciprocity and distributed feedback. When generative capacity, filtering power, and epistemic authority are centralized into a small number of market actors, the vector field ceases to circulate and begins to radiate asymmetrically, producing a one-to-many ontological broadcast layer that bypasses local meaning-making. This is not persuasion; it is field polarization. The result is not a shared ideology but coherence collapse through interference‚Äîthe ‚Äúnoisy, deceitful moment‚Äù Ward describes, where confusion is not a side effect of power but its operating condition.</p>
