<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">A differentiable field </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">: \mathcal{M} \to \mathbb{R}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> representing local semantic degrees of freedom. High </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">|</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">|</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> signifies evolving meaning; low </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">|</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">|</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> indicates stagnation or capture.</span></span>
