<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">lemma</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}[Predictive Capture Implies Entropic Collapse]</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">If an external optimizer enforces </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\arg\min_{\mathbf{v}} \mathbb{E}[\text{uncertainty}]</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">, then </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \to </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> and the system enters a capture region.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">lemma</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">proof</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Consider a recommendation algorithm minimizing prediction error on user clicks. Uncertainty is proxied by cross-entropy loss </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathcal{L} = -</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\sum</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> p_i \log q_i</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">. Minimizing </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathcal{L}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> constrains the distribution </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">q</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> to match </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">p</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">, reducing variance in semantic exploration. In RSVP, this maps to </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> evolving under </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\dot{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">} = -</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\eta</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \frac{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\delta</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \mathcal{L}}{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\delta</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">, driving </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> to a local minimum where </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> = </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">. Vector flow </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathbf{v}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> aligns to high-reward paths (e.g., outrage content), inducing </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \cdot</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \mathbf{v} &gt; </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> at engagement sinks. Example: TikTok's For You Page traps users in echo loops, flattening </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> over time.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">proof</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
