<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">By continuity, </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\frac{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\partial</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \rho</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">}{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\partial</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> t} + </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \cdot</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> (</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\rho</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \mathbf{v}) = </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> for density </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\rho</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">. Positive divergence at corporate nodes (e.g., Meta's ad platform) sources influence without sinks elsewhere, radiating </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathbf{v}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> outward. This diffuses </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> via coupling </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\dot{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">} </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\propto</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> -\mathbf{v} </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\cdot</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">, eroding gradients. Example: Centralized content moderation by a few firms creates global broadcast asymmetry, diminishing local semantic innovation on fringe platforms.</span></span>
