<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\author</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Flyxion}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\date</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{November 07, 2025}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">document</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\maketitle</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">abstract</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Jacob Ward‚Äôs thesis that AI-driven behavioral science increasingly constructs a ‚Äúworld without choices‚Äù</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">identifies a genuine transformation of governance, agency, and social autonomy. However, Ward‚Äôs model</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">implicitly assumes centralized persuasion and hierarchical capture. In this manuscript, we demonstrate</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">that this assumption mischaracterizes the dominant 21st-century failure mode. Using the</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">Relativistic Scalar‚ÄìVector Plenum</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} (RSVP) formalism, we show that modern behavioral capture is not</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">producing singular authoritarian control, but </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">entropic authoritarianism</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}‚Äîa distributed collapse of</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">semantic gradients driven by algorithmic microsurveillance, fragmented influence attractors, and the</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">erosion of coherent agency.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">We prove key results including: (1) a closed-form capture threshold </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\beta</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_c</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">, (2) the equivalence between</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">predictive optimization and gradient collapse, (3) the instability of monopolar attention fields,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">and (4) the condition under which agency turbulence becomes more dangerous than agency domination.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">This work integrates theoretical foundations from thermodynamics, information theory, predictive</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">processing, network dynamics, and political theory to provide a mathematically grounded critique of</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">behavioral AI as a phase transition in collective cognition rather than a traditional power consolidation.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">We conclude that the dominant risk mode is the topological death of meaning, not the centralization of it.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">abstract</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
