<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">proof</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Consider the semantic phase space volume </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">V(t) = </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\int</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> |</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">| </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\,</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> d</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\mu</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">. Under the RSVP flow </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\eqref</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{eq:phi_capture}--</span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\eqref</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{eq:v_capture} with constraints, the Liouville theorem for incompressible agency flow (</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \cdot</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \vec{v} = </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">) and bounded damping yields:</span></span>
