<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(106, 153, 85);">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\chapter</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{LLMs as Low-Curvature Semantic Surfaces}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Semantic curvature is defined as:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\[</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathcal{K} = \det(</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">^</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">2</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\]</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Human discourse exhibits mixed curvature (</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathcal{K} &gt; </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> generative regions, </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathcal{K} &lt; </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> exploratory regions).</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">LLMs exhibit:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\[</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathcal{K}_{LLM} </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\approx</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);"> 0</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\]</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">indicating </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textit</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">flat generativity</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}: high-volume continuation, low semantic acceleration.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The key pathology:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">itemize</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\item</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> High </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">token entropy</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\item</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> Low </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">agency entropy</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\item</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> Minimal effective curvature</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">itemize</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Thus:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\[</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\text{LLM output} </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\equiv</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \text{semantic foam without gradient}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\]</span></span>
