<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Related Work}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Concerns over the impact of algorithmically mediated choice arise from multiple intellectual traditions. The political economy of persuasive platforms has been extensively analyzed under the framing of filter bubbles and echo chambers, where recommenders reduce epistemic diversity and amplify selective exposure \cite{pariser2011filter,nguyen2020echo,chaney2018filterBubble,huszar2022algorithmic}. These critiques diagnose a narrowing of discourse but do not formalize how possibility itself becomes dynamically unavailable, nor do they model the collapse of agency as a systemic phase transition.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Causal and information‚Äìgeometric approaches have provided machinery for reasoning about representations without assuming a fixed coordinate system \cite{peters2017elements,amari2016infoGeometry}. These tools underpin basis-agnostic notions of divergence, intervention, and semantic distance, yet are not typically applied to the dynamics of collective cognition or to societal-scale autonomy loss. In parallel, work on attention topology and diffusion over interaction networks demonstrates that online agency is highly structured, path-dependent, and prone to bottlenecking \cite{zhu2021attention,verma2023agency,barabasi1999scale}. These results support the modeling of agency as a non-conservative flow field, but they do not characterize the consequences of extreme divergence or capture of that flow.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">A growing body of literature identifies structural pathologies in optimization-driven environments, including representational collapse, proxy overfitting, and gradient leakage under adversarial pressure \cite{geiping2022gradient,grunwald2022collapse,bak2012selforganized}. This work provides empirical grounding for the claim that sufficiently strong optimization pressure can erase internal degrees of freedom. However, these studies focus primarily on model dynamics rather than the collapse of cognitive possibility in populations interacting with such models.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Ethical critiques of recommender systems further highlight the incompatibility between engagement-maximizing objectives and epistemic health \cite{dwork2020fairness,noble2018algorithms,pennycook2021misinfo}. While these contributions motivate design corrections centered on fairness, welfare, or misinformation mitigation, they lack a unifying mathematical description of autonomy loss as a collapse of traversable meaning-space. Moreover, formal limits on unsupervised decomposition and clustering \cite{kleinberg2015impossibility} imply that any attempt to measure or discretize semantic space imposes non-neutral topology, reinforcing the need for observer-invariant formulations.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">In contrast to these literatures, the Relativistic Scalar‚ÄìVector Plenum (RSVP) framework offers:</p>
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">A dynamical theory of autonomy in which meaning and agency are fields, not attributes;</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">A phase transition model of capture, indexed by a critical ratio between semantic diffusion and optimization pressure;</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">A distinction between centralized control and entropic authoritarianism, formalizing the latter as multi-point agency divergence without coherence;</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">A prescriptive inversion for restorative systems, optimizing for preserved cognitive phase volume rather than predictive compression;</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">A basis-agnostic measurement proposal grounded in interventional semantic distance, avoiding coordinate-dependent embeddings.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">By unifying these elements, RSVP reframes algorithmic influence not as persuasion within a fixed space of meanings, but as a regeometry of the space itself. The consequence is a shift from normative arguments about user welfare to structural arguments about the conservation and dissipation of possible minds under external optimization pressure.</p>
