<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\]</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">On a domain of size </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">L</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">, the lowest nonzero mode is:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\[</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">k_{\min} = \frac{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\pi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">}{L}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\]</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Thus the transition point </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\beta</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_c</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> satisfies:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\[</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> = -D_</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \left(\frac{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\pi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">}{L}\right)^</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">2</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> - </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\beta</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_c</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\]</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\[</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\boxed{ </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\beta</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_c = \frac{D_</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \pi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">^</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">2</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">}{L^</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">2</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">} }</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\]</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">This gives a concrete, measurable collapse threshold in terms of:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">table</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}[htbp]</span></span>
