<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">where </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\gamma</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> is an Eckhaus-like factor determined by the reference semantic amplitude and pattern wave number, and </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">D_m(</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\psi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">)</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> is a cross-diffusion term proportional to </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Gamma</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_{\rm P}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> arising from coupling to attention flow. The exact coefficients depend on the background pattern </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> and can be computed by the same projection method used in Ref. </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\cite</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{pisegna2025nonreciprocal}. The important structural facts are:</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">enumerate</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">  \item</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> $</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Gamma</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_{\rm P}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> produces a wave-number independent contribution to growth/damping analogous to </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\lambda</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> in the h-NRCH model.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">  \item</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> For a given </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Gamma</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_{\rm P}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> there exists a critical semantic wavelength </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">q_E</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> (an RSVP Eckhaus threshold) below which particular perturbation directions destabilize.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">  \item</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> Nonreciprocal agency (</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\alpha</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_{\rm A}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">) can stabilize otherwise unstable regimes, creating a disorder‚Üíordered transition controlled by </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\alpha</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_{\rm A}/|</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Gamma</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_{\rm P}|</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">enumerate</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Practical implementation: use the same pseudospectral simulation recipe and linear-stability matrix construction as in h-NRCH to compute </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Lambda</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\psi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">)</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">, </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">v_g(</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\psi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">)</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> and </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">D_{\rm eff}(</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\psi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">)</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> numerically for RSVP parameter choices; see the Supplemental Material of the h-NRCH paper for an explicit algorithm.</span></span>
