<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Historical Arc of Behavioral Capture}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The trajectory from pre-digital persuasion to algorithmic capture spans over a century. Edward Bernays, applying Freudian psychology to mass manipulation in the 1920s, formalized propaganda as the "engineering of consent" \cite{bernays1928propaganda}. The Cambridge Analytica scandal of 2018 revealed how microtargeted political advertising weaponized behavioral data at scale. TikTok‚Äôs algorithm, by 2023, demonstrated real-time preference shaping through continuous engagement loops.</p>
