<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Stability Guarantee for Restored Autonomy}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{theorem}[Restoration Stability]
Let the composite operator <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">R</mi><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G} = \mathcal{R}\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7805em; vertical-align: -0.0972em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.0593em;">G</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">R</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span></span></span></span>.
Then autonomy is restored and remains stable if:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>œÅ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">    0 &lt; \rho(\mathcal{G}) &lt; 1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6835em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&lt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">œÅ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.0593em;">G</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&lt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span></span>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">and the diffusion‚Äìdamping balance condition holds:</p>
