<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Where </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathbb{P}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> projects onto divergence-controlled flows.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Interpretation:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">* </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">^</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">2</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> ‚Äî diffusion of meaning into adjacent possibilities</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">* </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">V'(</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">)</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> ‚Äî cultural priors pulling toward known narratives</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">* </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \cdot</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \mathbf{v}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> ‚Äî influence injection or extraction</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">* </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">-</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> ‚Äî natural sense-making flow</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">When optimization systems (e.g., recommender engines) minimize surprise, they introduce a field forcing:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\[</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\dot{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">} </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\propto</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> -</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \mathcal{F}_{\text{predictive}}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\]</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">which drives semantic gradients toward zero ‚Äî precisely the ‚Äúworld without choices‚Äù Ward warns about.</span></span>
