<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">An AI system is autonomy-preserving if and only if it satisfies:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">align</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">    \mathbb{E}[</span><span style="color: rgb(215, 186, 125);">\|</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(215, 186, 125);">\|</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">] </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">&amp;</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">&gt; </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);"> &amp;</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\text{(creates new distinctions)} </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">    \mathbb{E}[</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \cdot</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \mathbf{v}] </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">&amp;</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\approx</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);"> 0</span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);"> &amp;</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\text{(avoids funneling)} </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">    \mathbb{E}[</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \times</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \mathbf{v}] </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">&amp;</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">&gt; </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);"> &amp;</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\text{(supports option rotation)} </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">    \rho</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">(\mathcal{R}\mathcal{C}) </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">&amp;</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">&lt; </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">1</span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);"> &amp;</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\text{(stable autonomy basin)} </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">align</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">This defines a testable anti-capture specification.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\section</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Summary}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">itemize</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">    \item</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> Restoration is a distinct operator, not the absence of capture.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">    \item</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> It must overpower capture spectrally, not merely oppose it rhetorically.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">    \item</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> Stability demands stronger diffusion than flattening and stronger damping than funneling.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">    \item</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> Autonomy cannot be ‚Äúrecovered for free‚Äù ‚Äî it has a thermodynamic and computational cost.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">    \item</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> A system that does not inject agency curl will always reconverge to capture.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">itemize</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
