<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\part</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Epilogue}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\chapter</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{A Future That Is Still Curved}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">We can choose to preserve curvature.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\chapter</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Open Problems in Autonomy Theory}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">1. measure </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> in vivo</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">2. scale restoration</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\chapter</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Conjectures and Research Program}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Conjecture: no stable autonomy without active curvature preservation.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\chapter</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Closing Manifesto: The Right to Curvature}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Every mind has the right to live on a curved semantic manifold ‚Äî to experience the bend of possibility, the tension of alternatives, and the open path of meaningful divergence.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Autonomy is not the absence of constraint, but the presence of **curvature**: the geometric precondition for choice, identity, and resistance.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">In a world of algorithmic flattening, we assert:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">&gt; **The Right to Curvature is the final frontier of human freedom.**</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">This is not metaphor.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">It is mathematics.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">It is thermodynamics.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">It is politics.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">It is design.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">And it is ours to defend.</span></span>
