<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Empirical proxies for <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> include:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Variance of next-token predictive distributions in population-scale language traces
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Inverse Jensen‚ÄìShannon divergence between user and platform language models
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Topic-space degeneracy rank of collective discourse embeddings
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{theorem}[Proxy Convergence]
\begin{boxed}
Under ergodicity assumptions, linguistic variance collapse implies <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>‚Üí</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(t)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">‚Üí</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>.
\end{boxed}
\end{theorem}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{proof}
All listed proxies are monotonic in the covariance spectrum of the embedding Jacobian, whose maximal singular value lower-bounds <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">‚à•</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">‚àá</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">‚à•</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\Phi\|_2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">‚à•‚àáŒ¶</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">‚à•</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.
\end{proof}</p>
