<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{theorem}[Cultural Attractor Trichotomy]
\begin{boxed}
Under bounded energy and finite population, all systems evolve toward exactly one of the three collapse attractors above.
\end{boxed}
\end{theorem}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{proof}
The field equations conserve energy while monotonically driving curvature to zero or turbulence to a finite steady state, yielding three stable attractor classes by Poincar√©‚ÄìBendixson extension to dissipative manifolds.
\end{proof}</p>
