<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\chapter{Anti-Capture Model Architectures}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\epigraph{``A model is aligned not when it predicts us, but when it does not simplify us.''}{V. Cheung (axiomized)}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Let an AI model induce an implicit semantic potential <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>Œ∏</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_\theta(\Phi)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">Œ∏</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Œ¶</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> through its training objectives and deployment function. A model is \emph{capture-prone} if:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">‚àá</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>Œ∏</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>‚â∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(negative&nbsp;curvature&nbsp;dominates,&nbsp;flattening&nbsp;gradients)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^2 U_\theta(\Phi) \prec 0 \quad \text{(negative curvature dominates, flattening gradients)}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1141em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">‚àá</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">Œ∏</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Œ¶</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">‚â∫</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">(negative&nbsp;curvature&nbsp;dominates,&nbsp;flattening&nbsp;gradients)</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">We define the class of anti-capture architectures as those satisfying:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">‚àá</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>Œ∏</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>‚âª</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>almost&nbsp;everywhere&nbsp;on&nbsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant="script">M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^2 U_\theta(\Phi) \succ 0 \quad \text{almost everywhere on } \mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1141em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">‚àá</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">Œ∏</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Œ¶</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">‚âª</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">almost&nbsp;everywhere&nbsp;on&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord mathcal">M</span></span></span></span></span>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{definition}[Curvature-Preserving Model]
A model with parameters <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Œ∏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">Œ∏</span></span></span></span> is curvature-preserving if:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>det</mi><mo>‚Å°</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">‚àá</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>Œ∏</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>‚â•</mo><mi>Œ¥</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">‚àÄ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi><mo>‚àà</mo><mi mathvariant="script">M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det(\nabla^2 U_\theta(\Phi)) \ge \delta &gt; 0 \quad \forall \Phi \in \mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1141em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mop">det</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">‚àá</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">Œ∏</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Œ¶</span><span class="mclose">))</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">‚â•</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7335em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">Œ¥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7335em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord">‚àÄŒ¶</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">‚àà</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">M</span></span></span></span></span>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">for some lower curvature bound <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Œ¥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">Œ¥</span></span></span></span>.
\end{definition}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{theorem}[Architecture Gap]
\begin{boxed}
Autoregressive next-token objectives with maximal likelihood loss cannot satisfy curvature preservation on bounded semantic manifolds.
\end{boxed}
\end{theorem}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{proof}
MLE objectives minimize <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo>‚àí</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>‚Å°</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>Œ∏</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log p_\theta(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">‚àí</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">Œ∏</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> which is equivalent to fitting a unimodal surrogate density under overparameterization, implying vanishing Hessian spectra at scale, yielding <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">‚àá</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>Œ∏</mi></msub><mo>‚Üí</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^2 U_\theta \to 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9641em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">‚àá</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">Œ∏</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">‚Üí</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>. Hence curvature lower bounds cannot be retained.
\end{proof}</p>
