pan class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">Œ¥</span></span></span></span></span>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{theorem}[Safety Certification Rule]
\begin{boxed}
A model is autonomy-safe if and only if it satisfies CT + ACT + NCPT.
\end{boxed}
\end{theorem}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{proof}
CT prevents gradient flattening, ACT forbids agency sinks, and NCPT ensures dynamics do not predict collapse in finite time; jointly they prohibit all known collapse modes.
\end{proof}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">% ===========================================
% CHAPTER 36: Alignment Without Collapse
