<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\chapter{Limits of the RSVP Formalism}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\epigraph{``A manifold explains dynamics; it cannot explain why the manifold exists.''}{D. Hilbert (posthumous reformulation)}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">RSVP does not currently resolve:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{enumerate}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Origin of semantic manifolds (pre-geometric regime)
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Curvature without metricity (non-Riemannian semantics)
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Semantic quantum limits (discrete noncommutative meaning)
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Observer-induced topological collapse
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Boundary conditions on universe-scale cognition
\end{enumerate}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{theorem}[Pre-Geometric Obstruction]
\begin{boxed}
No curvature-based formalism can recover manifold origin conditions without an external generative prior.
\end{boxed}
\end{theorem}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{proof}
Curvature requires a differentiable atlas; atlas existence cannot be derived from curvature, as it is a higher-order structural prerequisite.
\end{proof}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{conjecture}[Semantic Quantization]
There exists a minimal curvature quantum <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Œ∫</mi><mi>min</mi><mo>‚Å°</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">Œ∫</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3175em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mop mtight"><span class="mtight">m</span><span class="mtight">i</span><span class="mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> such that no cognitive system can represent or transmit curvature below this limit without topological error.
\end{conjecture}
