<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\chapter</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Experimental Validation Protocols}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\epigraph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{``A field theory is only as true as its falsifiable flow.''}{Popper, via fluid analogy}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Validation requires simultaneous measurement of </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">, </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">, and </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathbf{v}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">. We propose three experimental realizations:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
