<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">document</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\maketitle</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">abstract</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Across journalism, public discourse, and critical technology studies, Jacob Ward‚Äôs warning that AI and behavioral science will conspire to automate choice has emerged as one of the most incisive diagnoses of emergent algorithmic power. However, Ward‚Äôs framework remains sociological in ontology and local in mechanism: it names the dangers but cannot formalize them as dynamical collapse modes, nor distinguish centralized authoritarian capture from multi-polar entropic fragmentation.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">This document reconstructs Ward‚Äôs thesis through the Relativistic Scalar--Vector Plenum (RSVP), a field-theoretic model of collective cognition in which semantic possibility evolves as a scalar entropy field </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">(x,t)</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> and agency propagates as a vector field </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathbf{v}(x,t)</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">. We demonstrate that ``a world without choices'' corresponds to degenerate field topology: </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\to </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> (semantic gradient collapse) and monopolar vector divergence </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla\cdot</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathbf{v} </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\gg</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);"> 0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> (agency centralization), a state we define as </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textit</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">entropic authoritarianism</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The manuscript contributes:</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">(1) a full formalization of behavioral capture as field collapse with Eckhaus stability analysis,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">(2) deep integration with Friston's Free Energy Principle, Maturana/Varela autopoiesis, and hydrodynamic nonreciprocity,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">(3) rigorous numerical stability bounds and active matter cognition analogs,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">(4) new design invariants for entropy-positive AI, and</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">(5) a reconstruction of the intellectual lineage leading to Ward‚Äôs claims, extended into a unifying thermodynamic ontology of governance, cognition, and power.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">abstract</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textbf</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214); font-weight: bold;">Keywords:</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} semantic collapse, entropic authoritarianism, nonreciprocity, active matter cognition, free energy principle, autopoiesis, hydrodynamic attention flow</span></span>
